WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.859
The production team for Game of Thrones had
some big shoes to fill when it came time to

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:09.350
cast Brienne of Tarth, and they pretty much
nailed it when they hired Gwendoline Christie

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.180
for the part.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.020
But even considering her natural aptitude
for the role, Christie had to put in a lot

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.000
of work to make the look perfect.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.200
Here's how the six-foot-three actress and
model got her body into the shape of a committed,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:22.960
lifelong warrior.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.840
Pre-audition training

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.360
Months before Brienne was introduced in season
two of the show, fans of the book series took

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.440
to the Internet and pegged Christie as an
ideal actor for the role.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.399
The online support is actually what pushed
her to try out for the role, and in the months

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.429
before the audition, she was already hitting
the gym to get herself in fighting shape.

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:48.379
Christie is one of the few performers remaining
in Game of Thrones' sprawling cast who is

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:53.160
actually on record as having read all of the
books, so she knew what kind of physique she'd

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.339
need to cultivate if she wanted a chance at
snaring the role.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.620
"I read the books and I really, really wanted
to play the part.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:05.200
I started kundalini yoga, kickboxing and running,
and completely changed my diet.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.600
I felt I wanted to undergo what was necessary
for the part."

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.160
Dance background

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.200
When it comes to working out, a background
in athletics goes a long way.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:19.580
Christie had a great foundation, acknowledging
in an interview with Stylist that "at a time"

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.500
she could have pursued a career as a professional
gymnast.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.420
"From the age of 7, I just loved dancing.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.560
I did ballet, tap, and rhythmic gymnastics.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.189
I did lots of dancing and was obsessed with
it.

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:32.460
I lived and breathed it."

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.960
"And then I had a back injury when I was 11
and had to stop."

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.760
The injury precipitated a change in interests,
which led to a career as an actress.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.700
But that early gymnastics background must
have helped her get her through the gruelling

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.120
training for Game of Thrones.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.580
Knight's training

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.580
One benefit of getting a high-profile role
on an expensive HBO production is that your

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.340
physique is going to get some serious Hollywood
help.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.020
In the early days of training, Christie worked
with trainers Phil Learney and Dalton Wong

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.600
to pack on muscle and learn how to use the
extra weight.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.159
She told Games Radar,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.200
"I was given extensive horse-riding lessons,
so that not only was I confident on the horse,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.320
but I could ride."

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.960
"My physicality was altered so I was much
heavier in the way I walked, less upright

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.100
and a lot more masculine."

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.100
That's a lot to go through, but Christie approached
it all with a true warrior's mentality.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.960
"I just dedicated myself to it entirely.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.860
There was no room for failure."

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.700
In the end, Christie lost 21 pounds and then
gained back about 14 in muscle, leaving her

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.960
dramatically stronger and more fit.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.480
Cold turkey

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.980
In the messed-up land of Westeros, a mug of
stiff ale is about the only way to get through

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:41.480
the day.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.020
But it's also a luxury the best knights have
to steer clear of.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.400
"Don't get drunk."

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:49.480
"No, m'lady."

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.590
To get into prime shape, Christie decided
to cut alcohol out of her diet completely,

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.320
along with other diet changes.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.320
She told Stylist:

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.300
"I completely changed my eating habits and
didn't drink for about two months, just in

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.820
the service of this part."

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.300
That's a big sacrifice, but it definitely
paid off.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.800
Acting the part

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.000
You've gotta love Brienne's spirit, but the
books rarely describe her looks in flattering

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:14.520
terms.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.850
"Do you think Lady Stark's going to want a
giant, toe-headed plank following her around

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:19.880
for the rest of her life."

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.940
So part of her training for Game of Thrones
involved learning how to look and move in

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.160
a more masculine way.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.100
Unlike Brienne, who feels at home in a suit
of armor, Christie is much more feminine,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.140
and she had to strip a lot of that away to
prepare for the Game of Thrones role, saying:

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.500
"I used to have really long blonde hair, always
wearing heels, lots of make-up.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.840
I had been someone who was highly feminized
and had chosen to look that way."

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.160
But as tough of that transition must have
been, Christie took it all in stride with

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.800
her characteristic optimism:

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:54.520
"I love a challenge, and I love defying limitation,
gender stereotypes and people's expectations

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:55.960
of me as an actress."

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.440
Real steel

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.380
Christie's training didn't stop when the cameras
started rolling.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.580
If anything, it intensified.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.200
According to an interview with Vogue, her
costume armor alone weighs 30 pounds, and

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.720
the sword isn't exactly a toy.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.060
Even in fights - like her epic battle with
the Hound in season 4 - Christie has to lug

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.320
all that weight around.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.630
In fact, she called that fight sequence "one
of the f****** hardest things I've ever done

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.140
in my life."

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:24.240
If that doesn't keep her in shape on its own,
it's definitely a motivator not to let her

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.260
physical conditioning slip.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.000
Fan loyalty

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:33.840
For all her hard work, Christie has been rewarded
with worldwide renown and an ever-more-successful

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.340
career.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.940
Former US President Barack Obama is on record
as a fan of the show who's flexed his authority

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.500
to find out what's going to happen to Brienne's
character between seasons.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:48.100
And in the celebrity world, pop singer Madonna
brought Christie specifically on stage to

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.920
compliment her in front of a crowd.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:55.180
For being a hard-working performer who put
in the extra effort to bring a beloved, inspiring

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.370
character to life, Christie deserves the admiration.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.100
Thanks for watching!

